WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.081 --> 00:00:05.430
Scrooge could hardly believe his eyes.

2
00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:15.119
His former partner, Jacob Marley, stood there looking like a ghost, metal chains wrapped all around his transparent body.

3
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.629
"What do you want from me, Marley?" Scrooge cried.

4
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:26.399
"I want many things from you." Marley's voice sounded exactly the same.

5
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.019
"In life, I was your partner, Jacob Marley."

6
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:37.234
"Yes." Scrooge felt his legs wobble.

7
00:00:37.235 --> 00:00:40.048
"Can you sit down?"

8
00:00:40.049 --> 00:00:42.168
"I can."

9
00:00:42.169 --> 00:00:48.546
"Let's both do it, then."

10
00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:51.296
The two of them sat near the fire.

11
00:00:51.297 --> 00:00:55.447
Scrooge continued to stare at the ghost in disbelief.

12
00:00:55.448 --> 00:00:57.635
Marley cocked his head.

13
00:00:57.636 --> 00:01:02.012
"You don't believe in ghosts, Ebenezer, do you?"

14
00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:05.939
"Not normally," Scrooge said.

15
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.447
"But tonight, so many strange things—"

16
00:01:09.448 --> 00:01:14.530
"Why do you doubt your senses?" Marley demanded.

17
00:01:14.531 --> 00:01:19.253
"Because little things can affect our senses," Scrooge said.

18
00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:28.167
"For example, you could be a hallucination caused by bad food I've eaten, like poorly cooked meat.

19
00:01:28.168 --> 00:01:34.820
Whatever you are, you do remind me more of gravy than a grave!"

20
00:01:34.821 --> 00:01:39.620
Scrooge rarely made jokes, for he had little sense of humor.

21
00:01:39.621 --> 00:01:44.634
But he was trying to keep down his terror in any way he could.

22
00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:49.594
The ghost of Jacob Marley was disturbing him to his bones.

23
00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:56.572
The figure moaned and shook his chains loudly, clearly not amused.

24
00:01:56.573 --> 00:02:01.462
Scrooge held on tightly to his chair to prevent himself from fainting.

25
00:02:01.463 --> 00:02:05.864
"Dreadful creature, why are you here?"

26
00:02:05.865 --> 00:02:12.070
"Do you believe in me or not?" Marley demanded.

27
00:02:12.071 --> 00:02:15.264
Scrooge closed his eyes.

28
00:02:15.265 --> 00:02:20.027
"I do. You are here so I must believe in you.

29
00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:23.703
But why have you come to me?"

30
00:02:23.704 --> 00:02:31.759
"I wear these heavy chains, which I made myself, link by link and yard by yard.

31
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.914
They are the result of the poor choices I made while alive."

32
00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:41.859
Marley glared at Scrooge with his awful eyes.

33
00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.361
"You have made the same choices, Ebenezer.

34
00:02:46.362 --> 00:02:49.777
You continue to make them."

35
00:02:49.778 --> 00:02:52.592
"Jacob," Scrooge said.

36
00:02:52.593 --> 00:02:58.638
"This is terrifying. Say something that will comfort me."

37
00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:03.199
"I have no comfort to give," Marley said.

38
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.979
"I am doomed to drag these chains with me as a ghost.

39
00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:14.444
It's my punishment for a lifetime of selfishness, pettiness, and greed."

40
00:03:14.445 --> 00:03:19.721
"But you were always so good at business," Scrooge said.

41
00:03:19.722 --> 00:03:23.688
"Business?" Marley scoffed.

42
00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:27.064
"Humans should have been my business!

43
00:03:27.065 --> 00:03:32.976
Charity, mercy, and kindness should have been my business. But,

44
00:03:32.977 --> 00:03:36.077
listen to me closely, Ebenezer. My

45
00:03:36.078 --> 00:03:38.997
time with you is short. And

46
00:03:38.998 --> 00:03:45.145
I'm here to warn you that you have only one chance of escaping the same fate. Tonight

47
00:03:45.146 --> 00:03:49.353
you will be haunted by three ghosts." Scrooge

48
00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:57.946
gulped. "More ghosts? I think I'd rather just go to bed!" "Without

49
00:03:57.947 --> 00:04:04.325
their visits, you are doomed to follow the same path that I walk. These

50
00:04:04.326 --> 00:04:09.139
ghosts will show you the way to save yourself. Expect

51
00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:13.057
the first one very soon. Good-bye,

52
00:04:13.058 --> 00:04:17.819
Ebenezer, and good luck." Marley

53
00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:24.927
backed away, clanking his chains and moaning. Scrooge

54
00:04:24.928 --> 00:04:29.539
cowered as the ghost floated out through the window. After

55
00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.881
Marley was gone, Scrooge hurried to the window. Outside,

56
00:04:34.882 --> 00:04:42.666
the air was filled with phantoms floating here and there, moaning as they went. Every

57
00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:46.739
one of them wore chains like Marley's ghost. Scrooge

58
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:53.371
went pale as he recognized some of his old business acquaintances. Turning

59
00:04:53.372 --> 00:05:00.599
away from the dreadful sight, he went to the door to make sure it was locked. Then,

60
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:06.807
holding his head in his hands, he went into his bedroom. He

61
00:05:06.808 --> 00:05:12.804
climbed into bed and fell asleep instantly. ***

62
00:05:12.805 --> 00:05:16.067
Scrooge woke up some time later.

63
00:05:16.068 --> 00:05:20.079
It was very dark, and the church bell was ringing.

64
00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:26.816
Scrooge counted the bell's chimes, expecting them to stop, as they always did.

65
00:05:26.817 --> 00:05:30.670
But they continued on and on.

66
00:05:30.671 --> 00:05:36.862
"How strange," Scrooge thought. "Am I dreaming?"

67
00:05:36.863 --> 00:05:42.506
At last, the chimes stopped, and a loud bong shook the walls.

68
00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:48.199
At the same moment, an eerie light filled the room.

69
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:53.918
Scrooge's eyes opened wide at the sight of a figure standing beside his bed.

70
00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:59.969
The figure was a strange combination of a young child and an old man.

71
00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.007
Its hair was long and white.

72
00:06:03.008 --> 00:06:07.757
But its face was smooth, without the slightest wrinkle.

73
00:06:07.758 --> 00:06:14.237
It wore a white tunic and held a fresh green holly branch in one hand.

74
00:06:14.238 --> 00:06:22.610
"I suppose you're one of the ghosts that Marley told me about?" Scrooge's voice shook as he spoke.

75
00:06:22.611 --> 00:06:29.112
"I am." The ghost's voice was soft and gentle.

76
00:06:29.113 --> 00:06:34.111
"Do you have a name?" Scrooge asked.

77
00:06:34.112 --> 00:06:38.499
"I am the Ghost of Christmas Past."

78
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:44.424
The spirit clasped Scrooge gently by the arm.

79
00:06:44.425 --> 00:06:52.891
"Arise and walk with me."

